From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: unisoc: gtelwifi: list every board revision in sprd,sc-id

postmarketOS builds dt.img with dtbTool-sprd from a single DTB
(deviceinfo_bootimg_qcdt_type="sprd"). dtbTool-sprd reads any number of
<chipset platform rev> triplets from sprd,sc-id and writes one table
entry per triplet, all pointing at the same blob. sboot picks the entry
whose platform equals hw_revision, so list all eight gtelwifi revisions
instead of patching one copy of the DTB per revision.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/unisoc/sc7730-samsung-gtelwifi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/unisoc/sc7730-samsung-gtelwifi.dts
@@ -212,10 +212,14 @@
 	compatible = "samsung,gtelwifi", "sprd,sc7730";
 
 	/*
-	 * Board id the Spreadtrum bootloader matches against dt.img.
-	 * The build script generates one copy per hardware revision.
+	 * Board ids the Spreadtrum bootloader matches against dt.img,
+	 * <chipset board-revision soc-revision>, one per known gtelwifi
+	 * board revision. dtbTool-sprd writes one dt.img entry for each
+	 * triplet, all pointing at this one DTB.
 	 */
-	sprd,sc-id = <8830 11 0x20000>;
+	sprd,sc-id = <8830 2 0x20000>, <8830 3 0x20000>, <8830 4 0x20000>,
+		     <8830 5 0x20000>, <8830 6 0x20000>, <8830 9 0x20000>,
+		     <8830 10 0x20000>, <8830 11 0x20000>;
 
 	/* fixed host numbers: the eMMC must stay mmcblk0 (init, tabflash) */
 	aliases {
